Make a full reset (RIS) clear the foreground, background, and cursor colors a program set with
OSC 10, 11, and 12.

Phi needs this because it tells clients which colors a program changed, and a client shows its own
theme for the rest. Upstream resets only the palette on RIS, like xterm and VTE, so a client would
keep a program's colors after a reset. tmux and Zellij clear a pane's colors on RIS, and Phi does
the same. The defaults the host set stay in place.

Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/discussions/14627

--- a/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
@@ -4966,6 +4967,9 @@ pub fn fullReset(self: *Terminal) void {
     };
     self.setCursorStyle(.default);
     self.colors.palette.resetAll();
+    self.colors.foreground.reset();
+    self.colors.background.reset();
+    self.colors.cursor.reset();
 
     // Always mark dirty so we redraw everything
     self.flags.dirty.clear = true;
